{"id": "EUVD-2026-103458", "enisaUuid": "7f5030ab-d0c4-3e76-ba9a-182ceecde791", "description": "WhoDB 0.104.0 before 0.135.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows remote attackers to read and write arbitrary host files by running DuckDB filesystem functions through the query editor. Attackers can log in to a DuckDB file without credentials and use read_text, read_blob, COPY ... TO or ATTACH to steal session.key and stored database credentials or overwrite files.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T02:14:25", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/clidey/whodb/security/advisories/GHSA-x3h5-pr45-fx4r", "https://github.com/clidey/whodb/commit/80111c9ebc2eec382222629ba9fd26236f1a40e6", "https://github.com/clidey/whodb/releases/tag/0.135.0", "https://github.com/clidey/whodb/blob/0.134.0/core/src/plugins/duckdb/duckdb.go#L375-L387", "https://github.com/clidey/whodb/blob/0.134.0/core/src/plugins/duckdb/db.go#L73-L95", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/whodb-0.104.0-before-0.135.0-arbitrary-file-read-write-via-duckdb-query-editor"], "aliases": ["GHSA-ch4j-xm23-vmm2", "CVE-2026-112005"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.57, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f5cc26a0-9037-3566-ac39-f6de3fda1d81", "product": {"name": "whodb", "vendor": {"name": "clidey"}}, "product_version": "0.104.0 <0.135.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9d271faf-8911-325b-98d4-6655d264a559", "vendor": {"name": "clidey"}}], "isExploited": false}